  "source_text": "wæscestre, an; f. One who washes. (l) used of a man :-- Iobinus wæs mín wæscestre (fullo), Gr. D. 191, 23 : 192. (2) of a woman :-- Hé wæs lufigende his wæscestran (presbyteram) swá swá his ágne swuster . . . þá þá hine geseah seó his wæscestre, Gr. D. 276, 1-14. [Þis us doð to understonden þe forbisne of þe wasshestren quod melius patefacit exemplar lotricum, O. E. Hml. ii. 57, 22.]"
